## Context
The author asked (2026-10-27) to reword `skills/hunt/SKILL.md`. Its eleven
numbered steps read as a fixed procedure, while the plan should choose what
runs: steps 6-8 assume the ticket is code (TDD), steps 10-11 assume a forge
(push, merge request, CI, `/gaze <pr>`), and Triage sits as a step instead of
being the planning phase. Local-only projects (e.g. arena: no remote, lands by
`git merge --no-ff`) and prose tickets fall outside the script.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Hunt is phrased as phases `[Plan]` `[Execute]` `[Verify]` `[Celebrate]`, not an eleven-step script
- [ ] Triage is promoted into Plan; the plan is announced with a brief justification before Execute
- [ ] Execute follows the plan; TDD applies to code only; prose takes no TDD and no word-pin tests
- [ ] Verify lands by the project's route: forge (push, merge request, CI, gaze) or local (the project's merge recipe), never assumed
- [ ] Plan names the monster route: a complex or multipart ticket goes back to the hunt's caller with a proposed decomposition (tracker, children, waves); the caller, author or raid, splits it, and raid handles a monster returned mid-wave
- [ ] `§ Worktree` anchors cited by `rules/claude-code.md` and `skills/raid/SKILL.md` still resolve
- [ ] Coder profile charter and the claude-code.md `/hunt N` phase label agree with the new wording
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes

## Relevant files
- `skills/hunt/SKILL.md`
- `profiles/coder/PROFILE.md`
- `rules/claude-code.md`

## Test
Wording change: no new tests (no word-pin tests). Existing guards that read
hunt (`tests/test_launch_model_choice.py`, `tests/test_agent_profiles.py`,
`tests/test_raid_invokes_hunt.py`) must stay green.
